# Auto-commit after each task milestone

When you finish a **fix**, **feature slice**, **style change**, or any discrete sub-task the user asked for:

1. Run `.\commit.bat` with an appropriate message (`feat:`, `fix:`, `style:`, `chore:`, or `docs:`).
2. Do this **before** starting the next sub-task in the same conversation.
3. Do **not** add co-authors — commits are solo (Avashik only).

If there is nothing to commit, skip and continue.

See `incremental-commits.mdc` for full workflow details.
